<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Barclay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1648">1648</a>–<a href="/years/1690">1690</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Barclay was a Scottish Quaker theologian whose Apology for the True Christian Divinity became the classic statement of Quaker belief. In 1682 he was one of the 24 proprietors who bought East Jersey, and he was made its governor for life, though he never went to America and ruled through deputies. He encouraged Scottish settlement in the colony.</p></div>
